  "step5_question": {
    "question": "What were the key outcomes of the solvency analysis for JPMorgan Chase as of September 30, 2026?",
    "ground_truth_answer": "The key findings from the solvency analysis of JPMorgan Chase as of September 30, 2026, include:\n- Debt Equity Ratio: 12.67 (total liabilities $4,719,177 million / total stockholders' equity $372,368 million)\n- Interest Coverage Ratio: 0.77 (income before income tax expense $20,134 million / total interest expense $26,020 million, three months ended September 30, 2026; on an EBIT basis, i.e. pre-tax income plus interest expense, the ratio is 1.77)\n- Financial Leverage Ratio: 13.67 (total assets $5,091,545 million / total stockholders' equity)\n- Long-term Debt to Capitalization Ratio: 0.55 (long-term debt $460,160 million / (long-term debt + total stockholders' equity))\nThese ratios reflect the highly leveraged balance sheet typical of a large bank, where deposits and other liabilities fund most of the assets. Because interest expense is an operating cost for a bank, the low interest coverage ratio does not by itself indicate a solvency problem.",
